analysisWe need to produce an assert statement for the comment at end of previousClearBit method.

Comment: "If the starting index is greater than or equal to -1, then for every index greater than the result and less than or equal to the starting index, the bit at that index is set to true."

Let's parse: method previousClearBit(int fromIndex) returns index of previous clear bit (i.e., false) before or at fromIndex. The comment says: If starting index >= -1, then for every index i such that result < i <= fromIndex, the bit at i is true (i.e., set). So after method call, we need an assert that captures this property.

We need to use this.get(i) to check bits. The method returns int result (implicitly). So we need to assert: (fromIndex >= -1) => (\forall int i; result < i && i <= fromIndex; this.get(i) == true). Need to refer to result as \result. Also need to refer to fromIndex variable; it's a parameter. Use fromIndex.

Thus assert: assert (fromIndex >= -1) => (\forall int i; \result < i && i <= fromIndex; this.get(i)); but this.get returns boolean, true when bit is set. So we need this.get(i) == true, but we can just write this.get(i). In JML, boolean expression is fine. So:

assert (fromIndex >= -1) => (\forall int i; \result < i && i <= fromIndex; this.get(i));

But need parentheses for precedence: => lower priority, but we have parentheses.

Thus final answer.

